## Summary

I transformed the three research data files (`new-product.json`, `whitelist-updates.json`, `insights.json`) into a Hacker News-inspired multi-column HTML report for **2026-08-27**, containing all **62 items**: 9 new products, 15 whitelist updates, and 38 technical insights.

### Design highlights
- **Authentic HN aesthetic** — orange `#ff6600` top bar, `#f6f6ef` background, Verdana body text, numbered story list with accent-colored rank markers
- **3-column responsive grid** — New Products (40%) · Whitelist Updates (35%) · Technical Insights (25%), collapsing to 2 columns <1150px and single column <700px, with sticky column headers

### Content features per section
| Section | Structure |
|---|---|
| **New Products** | Clickable name + domain, description, category chip, date, sources, community quotes |
| **Whitelist Updates** | Title link to release notes, product badge (orange), color-coded update-type badges (release/feature/announcement/bugfix), summary clamped to 3 lines, sentiment-colored community quotes (+N more reaction counts) |
| **Technical Insights** | Compact entries: title + origin domain, editorial type tags (paper/opinion/discussion/tutorial), author, points where applicable, topic hashtags |

### Quality verification (all passed)
- ✅ Valid HTML5 with balanced tags (parser-checked)
- ✅ **All 62 source URLs preserved** as functional links; zero missing
- ✅ Proper heading hierarchy (1×h1 → 3×h2 → 62×h3), skip-link, ARIA labels, focus-visible outlines
- ✅ All dates rendered as YYYY-MM-DD; no unescaped entities
- ✅ Print styles: single-column, unclamped text, page-break protection inside stories
- ✅ Zero external dependencies — instant load, works offline

